WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:10.026
This is how AI works in Ruvano. It reads what's already on your board, and helps in three places. It only suggests. It never changes your work by itself.

2
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:25.420
An admin turns AI on or off for the whole workspace, on the Team page. It says exactly what goes to the AI provider: card titles, notes, and pull request titles. Never emails, or passwords.

3
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:38.058
Reality check found a pull request that shipped without a card. Click, find its card. AI reads the pull request title and the cards on the board, and suggests the one it most likely completes.

4
00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:55.215
If it's right, link it. The pull request goes on that card, and the card moves to done, just as if the pull request had mentioned it.

5
00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:07.469
For a pull request that doesn't fit any card, like this tooling upgrade, AI says it couldn't find a match, instead of guessing. You can still add it as a done card yourself.

6
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:32.997
In standup, click, A I summary. It writes a few sentences from the board and today's notes, starting with whoever needs help. Edit it if you like, then copy it into your team chat.

7
00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:56.106
And on the shared status page, managers and clients get a short summary at the top, refreshed every few hours. It's marked as written by AI, and the exact lists stay right underneath.

8
00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:06.667
That's AI in Ruvano. It suggests and summarises, only from what's already on your board. Your team stays in control, and an admin can switch it off at any time.
